{{Term/Store|Highland Sheep|Highland Sheep|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Highland Sheep'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Highland Sheep'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Highland Sheep}}
Highland Sheep are timid [[Creature]]s that are known to gather in herds.<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|Originally native to the mountainous regions, these sheep were domesticated for their wool and have since found a home in villages. Once the fluffy wool grows out, it's harvested and used to make clothing and bedding. They're calm, timid creatures and move about in small herds.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> They are often found in pastures alongside [[Hateno Cow]]s and [[White Goat]]s, particularly at [[Hateno Pasture]] and certain [[Stable]]s. Originally, Highland Sheep lived in the mountains, but they have since been domesticated.<ref name="Compendium"/> This is because of their wool, which is harvested in order to craft clothes and bedding.<ref name="Compendium"/> Highland Sheep are herbivorous and will eat certain [[Material]]s, such as herbs, [[Fruit]]s, and vegetables, if they are nearby.

Recently, Hateno Pasture has had issues with [[Monster]]s coming up from [[Hateno Beach]] to steal their Highland Sheep.<ref>{{Cite|Although... Fine. You seem harmless enough. Forgive me, I've just been on edge with all these monsters running around. They come up from {{Color BotW|Blue|Hateno Beach}} to steal my sheep. If someone doesn't do something soon, I won't have any left!|Koyin|BotW}}</ref> As part of "[[The Sheep Rustlers]]" [[Side Quest]], [[Link]] will find two Highland Sheep held captive at the [[Monster Stronghold]] on the Beach. After the Monsters have been defeated, the Sheep will disappear. Once this is done, [[Koyin]] will notice her Sheep are calmer, and she gives Link 10 bottles of [[Fresh Milk]] as a reward.<ref>{{Cite|I had a feeling. When the sheep all calmed down, I thought, "Maybe he did it..." So it seems I owe you some thanks. This isn't much of a reward, but hey, it's light. That counts for something.|Koyin|BotW}}</ref>

